/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (A file system is the method and data structure that an operating system uses to control how data is stored and retrieved. Without a file system, information placed in a storage medium would be one large body of data with no way to tell where one piece of information stops and the next begins. The Linux File System is a structured method of storing and organizing data on a Linux machine. It arranges files in a hierarchical directory format starting from the root directory \(/\). )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
